# AGENTS.md

This file guides agentic coding assistants for this repo.
Keep changes aligned with the project docs and rules.

## Sources of truth (must follow)
- `GEMINI.md` (AI collaboration guide and project constraints).
- `.cursorrules` (Cursor rules with external includes).
- `.cursor/rules/shared` (pointer to shared rule set).
- If present in the future: `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.

## Core project context
- Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 18 + TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (Radix primitives).
- Data for dashboard views is static JSON in `src/data/json/`.
- Access data via `src/services/` service layer.
- AI chatbot uses a database; dashboard UI does not.

## Build, lint, test, deploy
Use pnpm from repo root.

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm run dev
pnpm run build
pnpm run start
pnpm run lint
```

For Firebase deployment, always use the **Firebase Deployment Specialist** skill (OpenCode: skill({ name: "Firebase Deployment Specialist" }); Codex: load repository deployment instructions or request cross-client fallback) to ensure the correct build configuration is applied (especially for Node 24+ compatibility).

Unit test command (single test file):

```bash
pnpm run test
# or run a specific file
pnpm exec tsx --test src/lib/action-scoring.test.ts
```

Playwright (ai-chatbot) e2e tests:

```bash
# run from repo root
pnpm -C ai-chatbot exec playwright test
# run a single file
pnpm -C ai-chatbot exec playwright test tests/e2e/example.test.ts
```

Notes:
- Playwright config lives at `ai-chatbot/playwright.config.ts`.
- Web server is `pnpm dev` and expects `/ping` to respond.

## Required docs to read before large changes
- `docs/020-architecture.md`
- `docs/040-running-locally.md`
- `docs/060-vibe-coding-guidelines.md`
- `docs/070-rollback-instructions.md`

## Code style and formatting
- TypeScript strict mode is enabled (`tsconfig.json`).
- Use Prettier formatting (standard project settings).
- Prefer functional React components and hooks.
- Keep components small and single-responsibility.
- Reuse before rebuild; check existing components first.

### Imports
- Prefer path alias `@/*` for src imports.
- Group imports by: external, internal, relative, styles.
- Avoid deep relative paths when alias is available.

### File and symbol naming
- Components: PascalCase (`SolutionOverviewSection.tsx`).
- Files: kebab-case for general files and dashboards.
- Functions/variables: camelCase.
- Types/interfaces: PascalCase.
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for true constants.

### Types and data modeling
- Define shared types in `src/types/`.
- JSON data must map to typed interfaces.
- Prefer explicit types on public functions and props.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` with narrowing when needed.

### Error handling
- Fail fast with clear messages for invalid input.
- Use error boundaries for UI resiliency when appropriate.
- Keep error surfaces user-friendly and context-specific.

### UI and branding
- Preserve Army ARDAP branding and layout standards.
- Maintain logo spacing and presentation view layout.
- Keep SAFe terminology consistent in UI copy.
- Use "leading practice" or "recommended practice" wording
  instead of "best practice" (project terminology rule).

### Data and architecture constraints
- Dashboard data is static JSON under `src/data/json/`.
- Access JSON only through `src/services/` service functions.
- Keep dashboard UI decoupled from database code.
- AI chatbot database lives in `ai-chatbot/` and `src/lib/db/`.
- Prefer updating shared types when JSON shapes change.

## Testing guidance
- Test new or modified dashboard widgets in isolation first.
- Validate in one dashboard level before reusing widely.
- Prefer targeted tests before broader suites.

## AI collaboration rules (from GEMINI.md)
- Do not use the Google Antigravity agent browser for verification.
- Ask the user to validate UI changes in their browser.
- Follow Conventional Commits if you are asked to commit.
- Use git helper scripts:
  - `python scripts/git-inspect.py` for status/log/diff.
  - `python scripts/git-push-universal.py` for commits.

## Cursor rules summary (.cursorrules)
The `.cursorrules` file includes shared rule sets from a 
knowledge base outside this repo. Those includes cover:
- ClickUp workflow rules and task management.
- Git safe operations and terminal troubleshooting.
- Coding principles, file naming, delivery methodology.
- Brand voice guidelines and framework philosophy.
- MCP tool usage and background task monitoring.
If any rule conflicts exist, prefer `GEMINI.md` user section.

## Copilot rules
- No `.github/copilot-instructions.md` found in this repo.

## Safe defaults for agents
- Keep edits minimal and localized.
- Avoid database work for dashboard UI unless requested.
- Check `src/components/ui` and `src/components/dashboard`
  before creating new components.
- Respect Army ARDAP visual standards and accessibility.

## Common paths
- Pages and layouts: `app/`
- Components: `src/components/`
- Services: `src/services/`
- Types: `src/types/`
- Data: `src/data/json/`
- Styles: `styles/` and `app/globals.css`
- Scripts: `scripts/`

## When unsure
- Ask for clarification before making broad changes.
- Provide options and explain tradeoffs briefly.
